  (text "Limb: 4 low-side channels. Muscle wire k runs from the +10 V hole to hole Wk. W1/W2 and W3/W4 are the antagonist pairs." (at 20 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 666442fb-2eeb-47c5-afd9-13f2a6550d40))
  (text "Flyback diodes may be fitted DNP if the wire leads are short. Gate pull-downs keep every MOSFET off when the 74HC595 outputs are disabled." (at 20 34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid c0b63554-46cb-4d15-a72f-caec610b6eaa))
  (text "AO3400A pins: 1 G, 2 S, 3 D (SOT-23)." (at 20 38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1dc688ae-f6f5-47fa-81ba-fe23fbf774cd))
  (text "Gate guard (hardware, no software involved): CAC AC-couples the drive, RPD bleeds it, the BAT54 clamp restores the low level each cycle." (at 20 42 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 079cf28d-6692-4274-b8fb-60d9a77218e5))
  (text "Normal pulses (up to ~250 us) pass with a few percent droop; a gate stuck high decays below threshold in ~3 ms (22 nF x 100 k). Use 100 nF with IRLZ34N." (at 20 46 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid dd75c12d-d407-4e3b-9df1-e729d2a19687))
)
